Article 36

(1) The community may participate in the implementation of women's empowerment and protection.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, groups or social community organizations.

(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:

a. cooperation;
b. active role in policy formulation; and c. complaints/reports.
(4) The obligations and responsibilities of the community in the protection of women are implemented through activities:
a. conducting prevention of criminal acts;
b. providing protection to victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. assisting in the process of submitting an application for protection determination; and
e. providing information or reporting the occurrence of violent criminal acts to law enforcement officers.
(5) Further provisions regarding community participation as referred to in paragraph (3) are regulated in a Mayor Regulation.
